  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simplify the given product step by step. Let's start by simplifying each fraction in the product:\n\n1. Simplify each fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\log_k(5^{k^2-1})}{\\log_{k+1}(5^{k^2-4})}\n   \\]\n\n2. Use the change of base formula for logarithms:\n   \\[\n   \\log_a(b) = \\frac{\\log_c(b)}{\\log_c(a)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Substitute \\(a = k\\), \\(b = 5^{k^2-1}\\), and \\(c = 5\\) into the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\log_k(5^{k^2-1}) = \\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-1})}{\\log_5(k)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Substitute \\(a = k+1\\), \\(b = 5^{k^2-4}\\), and \\(c = 5\\) into the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\log_{k+1}(5^{k^2-4}) = \\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-4})}{\\log_5(k+1)}\n   \\]\n\n5. Substitute these simplified fractions back into the product:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\log_k(5^{k^2-1})}{\\log_{k+1}(5^{k^2-4})} = \\frac{\\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-1})}{\\log_5(k)}}{\\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-4})}{\\log_5(k+1)}} = \\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-1}) \\cdot \\log_5(k+1)}{\\log_5(5^{k^2-4}) \\cdot \\log_5(k)}\n   \\]\n\n6. Simplify the expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-1}) \\cdot \\log_5(k+1)}{\\log_5(5^{k^2-4}) \\cdot \\log_5(k)} = \\frac{(k^2-1) \\cdot \\log_5(k+1)}{(k^2-4) \\cdot \\log_5(k)}\n   \\]\n\n7. Notice that \\(k^2-1 = (k-1)(k+1)\\) and \\(k^2-4 = (k-2)(k+2)\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(k^2-1) \\cdot \\log_5(k+1)}{(k^2-4) \\cdot \\log_5(k)} = \\frac{(k-1)(k+1) \\cdot \\log_5(k+1)}{(k-2)(k+2) \\cdot \\log_5(k)}\n   \\]\n\n8. Combine all the fractions:\n   \\[\n   \\prod_{k=4}^{63} \\frac{(k-1)(k+1) \\cdot \\log_5(k+1)}{(k-2)(k+2) \\cdot \\log_5(k)}\n   \\]\n\n9. Simplify the product:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\log_5(5^3) \\cdot \\log_5(5^4) \\cdots \\log_5(5^{3968})}{\\log_5(5^2) \\cdot \\log_5(5^3) \\cdots \\log_5(5^{3965})}\n   \\]\n\n10. Notice that many terms cancel out:\n    \\[\n    \\frac{\\log_5(5^3) \\cdot \\log_5(5^4) \\cdots \\log_5(5^{3968})}{\\log_5(5^2) \\cdot \\log_5(5^3) \\cdots \\log_5(5^{3965})} = \\frac{\\log_5(5^{3968})}{\\log_5(5^2)} = \\frac{3968}{2} = 1984\n    \\]\n\n11. Therefore, the product is \\(1984\\), and since \\(1984\\) is already in its simplest form, \\(m = 1984\\) and \\(n = 1\\).\n\n12. Finally, \\(m + n = 1984 + 1 = 1985\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1985}\n\\]",
